title: Use the candidate's session host configuration in candidate validation

doc:
  - audience: [Node Dev, Runtime Dev]
    description: |
      Snapshots `max_pov_size` and `validation_code_bomb_limit` per session as
      a new `SessionExecutionConfig` primitive, stored in the `session_info`
      pallet (pruned with the dispute window) and exposed via a new
      `ParachainHost::session_execution_config` runtime API (v17).

      This PR fixes candidate-validation and prospective-parachains' PVD
      construction to key `max_pov_size` on the candidate's relay-parent
      session rather than the current host configuration. The
      `validation_code_bomb_limit` is read from the same per-session snapshot
      so the lookup is pruning-safe for cross-session disputes against
      candidates whose relay-parent block has been state-pruned.
      inclusion_emulator takes `max_pov_size` from the candidate's PVD instead
      of `constraints` when validating fragments. Pre-v17 runtimes fall back to
      previous behavior at every call site.

